{"id": "EUVD-2026-104296", "enisaUuid": "fea0adc3-7e86-3080-a4c6-9f51424e0c03", "description": "rdesktop through 1.9.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in process_plane() in bitmap.c that allows malicious RDP servers to crash clients by sending malformed 32 bpp compressed bitmaps. Attackers can declare a large bitmap geometry with a short compressed body in bitmap update PDUs or bitmap cache orders, causing unbounded reads past the receive buffer and denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:28:48", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/rdesktop-bitmap-decompress-oob-read", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/issues/436", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/pull/437", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/blob/v1.9.0/bitmap.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rdesktop-through-1.9.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-process-plane"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8gqw-q36r-ch2f", "CVE-2026-112277"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "876bc32b-75eb-39a7-861c-7e1ddee52175", "product": {"name": "rdesktop", "vendor": {"name": "RDesktop"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "121fb23c-a097-329f-b699-13edc8033f66", "vendor": {"name": "RDesktop"}}], "isExploited": false}